   "comment": "a fin inside a working cell costs the driver MORE than the same fin measured alone, because the cell's output swings against the input (Miller) and the internal nodes move with it. That excess is real energy and it is transistor, not wire -- but it is not capacitance sitting on the net, so the capacitance split above uses the static figure instead. The per-hold-state spread in by_cell_pin is the size of the Miller term: a cell whose output cannot move in either state (AO21x1 driven on A1, MAJx2) shows none.",
