   "why": "the bottom-up figure is a floor TWICE over (corrected Tue 27 Oct 2026 by Q129(a); it said three times): half the design's capacitance is unpriced (CTS and repair_design made those nets after the netlist was simulated), and the ledger covers one lane's arithmetic while the board pays for the register file's read ports, the operand bus, the result path and leakage as well. The third reason once given here -- that the between-cell wire has no coupling term -- is WITHDRAWN: the global-route Steiner estimate carries coupling already and runs 20-23% above the extraction, so extracting the wire moves 0.137 pJ OUT of 'accounted' and widens the gap (1.9465 -> 1.8094 pJ bottom-up, closure against the board 33.7% -> 31.3%). Of the two reasons that remain, the unpriced half got slightly worse on a routed design, 43.6% of the farads priced against 50.5%. See docs/reports/data/2026-10-27-q129-routed-netlist/.",
